1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,717
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,657
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
Then I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,260
We live in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,657
But we don't wanna live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:39,777
But we have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,820
We live in wonderland.

26
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:14,457
Ah, the snow, too bad.

27
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:16,900
Snow in this climate? Sure, why not?

28
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:20,797
Already happened once You just
missed it because you were asleep

29
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,540
Hey, what about you?

30
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:23,777
Do you think it's going to snow?

31
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:24,857
I wouldn't rule anything out.

32
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:28,357
But the sea you were in the
first time it snowed was special.

33
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:30,597
The seven magnetic fields
that emit from Reverse

34
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:33,621
Mountain tend to make
things particularly chaotic.

35
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:40,457
But that doesn't mean you should relax
your guard while sailing these waters.

36
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:44,305
The odds of it being as wild as
your first journey may be small.

37
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:49,117
Still, these waters aren't normal and are
certain to hold surprises of their own.

38
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:51,640
Remember, never underestimate the sea.

39
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:53,580
Hey, guys!

40
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:57,740
Anyone care to sample my special drink?

41
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:11,605
Hey, you guys want to
get out the fishing gear?

42
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:12,810
Fishing?

43
00:03:12,893 --> 00:03:13,877
Hell yeah, I'm in.

44
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:14,797
Sounds good to me.

45
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:17,097
I'll even make you one of
my custom fishing rods.

46
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:18,062
You'll love it.

47
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:21,997
Well, somebody's sure thirsty.

48
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:22,910
Have another.

49
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,440
Look at him go!

50
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,257
Yeah, give him another one!

51
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:31,928
They're acting like idiots!

52
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,475
Maybe this will help.

53
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:35,730
Just relax.

54
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:38,297
These boys may go through
their goofy phases,

55
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:40,457
but when things get
rough, they get to work.

56
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:42,020
Trust me, I should know.

57
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:44,557
Sorry, I don't know what's wrong with me.

58
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,699
I'm getting worked up over nothing.

59
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,984
This ship will put you at ease.

60
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,668
You'll cheer up in no time.

61
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:54,990
Attaboy!

62
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,380
Yeah, they're funny.

63
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:21,060
Hey, look, it's a dolphin,
pirate's best friend.

64
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,580
Whoa, beautiful!

65
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,840
It's huge!

66
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:38,600
Ha ha ha ha!

67
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,300
Let's go!

68
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,637
Move it!

69
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:53,940
Okay, going.

70
00:04:58,860 --> 00:04:59,740
Got it.

71
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:03,020
Take that side. Gotcha.

72
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:04,920
She was right.

73
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,400
Okay, hurry. Let's move.

74
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,040
Get ready.

75
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,040
It's gonna be a big one.

76
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,560
Nami, which direction now?

77
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,860
Give me a second, I'll check.

78
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,300
Port side, fall!

79
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:50,100
Turning fall!

80
00:06:12,340 --> 00:06:13,557
There's no mistake,

81
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:18,897
Cactus Island and this one here are
definitely pulling against each other.

82
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:20,620
Our next stop!

83
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:36,540
This is it, our second
island in the Grand Line?

84
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:56,640
Mr. Three?

85
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,660
Yes, my dear, hold on.

86
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:03,935
There's nothing quite like
the rich aroma of Earl Grey.

87
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,310
I'm bored.

88
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:08,797
On the one hand, you say you're bored.

89
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:11,586
On the other, you don't
like working, correct?

90
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,510
Mm-hmm.

91
00:07:12,593 --> 00:07:13,677
Then why don't you cease your complaining?

92
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:16,237
And revel in the enjoyment of
this rare slice of freedom,

93
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:18,677
Some circumstances have
generously afforded you.

94
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:21,407
How grand to be able to
take a long vacation.

95
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:24,520
A privilege few officers
ever get to indulge.

96
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:25,700
One more thing.

97
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:28,557
I would appreciate your
mindful and immediate

98
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:31,816
discretion in not calling
me by my codename in public.

99
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:35,237
Otherwise, people will
discover that I am indeed Mr.

100
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,150
Three.

101
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,390
Sure.

102
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:42,730
Incidentally,

103
00:07:42,813 --> 00:07:44,277
I couldn't help noticing
you've been perusing

104
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:46,717
that piece of paper over
the last several days.

105
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,212
Why does it grab you so?

106
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,852
It's an order from boss.

107
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:52,585
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

108
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,500
It says Mr.

109
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:58,091
Five has been taken down.

110
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:02,937
If someone had to be terminated, I wish it
would have been someone useless like Mr.

111
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:03,850
Two.

112
00:08:03,933 --> 00:08:06,505
So what would benefit
you with a fat promotion?

113
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,369
It's not that necessarily.

114
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:09,697
Rather, the downfall of Mr.

115
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,777
Five is hardly exciting news at all.

116
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:14,197
The man excelled at
nothing but his own idiocy,

117
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:17,456
clinging to his Devil Fruit
power like a drowning rat.

118
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:20,897
You are correct that a modicum
of my indifference stems

119
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:23,697
from the fact that Five's
misfortune brings me no gain.

120
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:27,662
All we may learn is power means
nothing if not properly harnessed.

121
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:37,177
Superior criminals are those who execute
their crimes using superior intellect.

122
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:39,025
Nevertheless, whoever beat Mr.

123
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,657
Five should be made an example of,

124
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:43,477
If for no other reason than to
preserve the reputation of terror,

125
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:46,097
our organization is
painstakingly cultivated,

126
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:48,415
and indeed for criminality as a whole.

127
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:02,157
I can see why they call
this place Little Garden.

128
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,220
I can't.

129
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,617
What's little about it?

130
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:07,337
Yeah, this island looks
pretty harsh if you ask me.

131
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:08,479
Why the cute name?

132
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:11,620
Yeah, it looks like a jungle out there.

133
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:14,097
Maybe we'd be better
off skipping this one.

134
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:15,010
We have to be careful.

135
00:09:15,093 --> 00:09:18,627
I can't help but remember the
warning Miss All Sunday gave us.

136
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:20,060
So what?

137
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:23,500
We might be attacked by
giant monsters? Who knows?

138
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:27,337
Listen, I'm sure we can make it to the next
island without going ashore on this one.

139
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:30,126
The only way to reset
the log is to go ashore.

140
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:33,357
Not to mention we're in dire need
of restocking our food supply.

141
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:36,197
We didn't get so much as a
sack of flour in the last town.

142
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:38,220
Guys, there's our ticket in.

143
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:40,330
Huh?

144
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,557
Think they'll have a
barbecue restaurant here?

145
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:49,457
We didn't travel all
this way for barbecue.

146
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:51,577
I thought the point of
this visit was to get food.

147
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:54,017
Food, as in supplies
we're going to cook later?

148
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:55,417
Jeez, what are you thinking?

149
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:56,440
I don't know.

150
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:58,916
Oofsop might be right about this one.

151
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:03,057
Just take a look at the
gargantuan plant life here.

152
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:06,199
I've never seen anything
like it, not even in books.

153
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,700
You're so adorable.

154
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:16,677
Thank you. That's not funny.

155
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:18,054
I was talking to Nami.

156
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:19,720
What was that screeching?

157
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:23,120
It's all right, love.

158
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,257
It's only a bird.

159
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:26,277
Perfectly harmless, just like this jungle.

160
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:27,713
Nothing to worry about.

161
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:30,870
What's wrong?

162
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:39,997
What the hell's the matter
with you, you damn bird?

163
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:42,180
Oh, it's big. Could be tasty.

164
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:47,730
Hear that?

165
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:51,625
Is that the kind of noise you
expect to hear in a normal jungle?

166
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:54,197
That sounded like a volcano erupting.

167
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,633
We're all going to die!

168
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,460
A tiger!

169
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:10,620
It's gigantic!

170
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:21,310
What?

171
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,969
Luffy, what just happened?

172
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:24,400
I know normal.

173
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:26,220
This is definitely not it.

174
00:11:26,820 --> 00:11:31,408
Someone explain to me how a mammoth tiger
can just keel over covered in blood?

175
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:34,465
Long bows and food, be damned!

176
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:37,157
We're not stepping foot on
that island and that's final!

177
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:39,597
We can still reset the
readings on the ship.

178
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:40,897
We'll just sit tight until then.

179
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:41,810
Right!

180
00:11:41,893 --> 00:11:43,837
When that's done, we'll
leave and never look back.

181
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:44,750
Great!

182
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:46,150
Yeah, great!

183
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,980
We'll all just stay here.

184
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:58,800
Sanji, go make lunch.

185
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:00,260
You want lunch?

186
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:02,120
Yep, and one more thing.

187
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:06,362
Make it a great big pirate lunch
with lots of meat and no veggies.

188
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:08,599
I'm going to need some more energy.

189
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,360
Energy for what?

190
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:11,297
What are you doing?

191
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:12,577
You're not leaving here.

192
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:13,490
You know.

193
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:16,081
Beast, do you want to come along?

194
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:18,250
It's you.

195
00:12:18,333 --> 00:12:19,417
I can't stop him.

196
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:20,794
He's too enthusiastic.

197
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:22,040
Is he crazy?

198
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:26,437
Somewhere out there is a monster big
enough to grind a tiger into base.

199
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:27,820
Saji, I'm starving.

200
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:29,617
Right, be patient.

201
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:32,112
and I'll have it to you as soon as I can.

202
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:37,957
Say, Luffy, would it be all
right if I come along with you?

203
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,700
Sure, sounds great. No!

204
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:41,857
Phoebe, you can't be serious!

205
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:45,817
Yeah, I'd rather not sit here with
nothing to do but worry about my troubles.

206
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:48,277
This will keep me busy
till the logs reset.

207
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:50,157
Out of the question, seriously!

208
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:52,217
It's way too dangerous for you out there!

209
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:53,130
I'll be fine.

210
00:12:53,213 --> 00:12:55,062
Besides, I'll have Karoo with me.

211
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:58,997
Hey, something's wrong.

212
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:00,557
Karoo doesn't look too good.

213
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:01,797
You might be in shock.

214
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:03,777
Vivi, if you go exploring,
you'll need to eat.

215
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:04,917
I'll pack you a lunch.

216
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:05,830
Thanks.

217
00:13:05,913 --> 00:13:08,157
While you're at it, could
you fix something for Karoo?

218
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,070
Of course.

219
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,692
You just leave it to me.

220
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,637
Now you're all set and ready to go.

221
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:29,661
two pirate lunches for Luffy and
Vivi and a special drink for Karoo.

222
00:13:29,820 --> 00:13:30,650
Thanks.

223
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:37,140
Well, see you guys later.

224
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:41,076
Don't worry, everything will be fine.

225
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:43,740
Vivi, what a girl.

226
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,260
She's so brave.

227
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:51,002
And just what would you expect from someone
who could infiltrate the enemy's ranks?

228
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:54,840
I'm bored. I'm gonna take a walk.

229
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:56,300
Take a walk?

230
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:00,360
Hey, Zoro.

231
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:01,850
Wait up.

232
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:05,357
You know we're kind of
short on food, right?

233
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:08,397
If you find any animals that
appear edible, bring them back.

234
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,620
Okay, it's easy.

235
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:11,717
I could see why you'd want to send me,

236
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:14,337
because I could bring back something
you couldn't catch yourself.

237
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:16,126
What the hell does that mean?

238
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:20,000
I won't let that remark go unchallenged.

239
00:14:20,180 --> 00:14:22,697
You're saying you can capture
bigger game than I can,

240
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:24,898
like my hunting skills are inferior?

241
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,200
Yeah, that's right.

242
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:34,258
Challenge accepted.

243
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:41,082
Okay, winner brings back
the most pounds of meat.

244
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:42,717
What do you mean pounds?

245
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:44,017
Because I'll bring back tons.

246
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:46,777
Why don't you let your hunting
do your talking for you?

247
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:47,920
Good luck, cook.

248
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,537
I will never understand it.

249
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:53,477
Why do those two jerks
have to be so competitive?

250
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:54,660
Don't cry.

251
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:59,293
If it makes you feel better, I'm just
as stumped by their behavior as you.

252
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:05,356
We're sitting ducks.

253
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:07,618
Don't you think I already know that?

254
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:13,920
Why didn't I think of that before?

255
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:16,576
Where are you going?

256
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,520
Nami, what's wrong?

257
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:21,600
That's not it.

258
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:25,740
Not this one either. Gah!
Gah! Nami! Whoa! Hey!

259
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,317
What the heck are you
looking for anyway, huh?

260
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:29,230
Quiet!

261
00:15:29,313 --> 00:15:31,395
I remember reading about it in a book.

262
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,637
Uh, reading about what?

263
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:34,640
Little garden.

264
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:39,737
Hey, what's the matter?

265
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:41,157
Over here, check it out.

266
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:43,652
It's a shellfish that looks like a squid.

267
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,360
Shell squidfish!

268
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:49,840
How strange.

269
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:52,121
It sort of assembles an amminoid.

270
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,180
Cool, huh?

271
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:08,280
I've got a feeling someone's
been following me for a while.

272
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,120
Couldn't be.

273
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,580
Can't you see I'm busy?

274
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:31,380
Paul Yee Koo!

275
