I don't know what you're supposed to
be, but I'm guessing you're edible.

276
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:52,017
Let me see, which one was it? Maybe...

277
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:54,797
I think I read it recently,
but I don't remember.

278
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,998
The title's on the tip of my tongue.

279
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:05,000
That's weird.

280
00:17:05,220 --> 00:17:07,102
What's a sea king doing on land?

281
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,000
A dinosaur!

282
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:14,350
Awesome!

283
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,900
No way! This is unreal!

284
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,310
Huh?

285
00:17:19,393 --> 00:17:23,647
Somehow this island has been frozen in
time, stuck in the age of the dinosaurs!

286
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:26,637
Travel in the Grand Line is so difficult,

287
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,957
so no species ever migrated
between the islands,

288
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:31,569
and their unique
ecosystems were preserved!

289
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:35,477
Some of these islands have developed
extremely sophisticated cultures,

290
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:37,640
both biological and sociological,

291
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:41,037
while others remain in a sort
of evolutionary stagnation with

292
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:44,477
little to no progression for several
thousands or tens of thousands,

293
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:45,390
or...

294
00:17:45,473 --> 00:17:48,040
In this case, it seems,
even millions of years.

295
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:52,617
I can only assume that
it's the random climates

296
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:54,957
within the Grand Line
that make this possible.

297
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:57,800
I mean, what other explanation is there?

298
00:17:57,920 --> 00:18:00,920
We're standing on the island
that predates mankind!

299
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:03,990
Luffy!

300
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:08,500
Are you insane?

301
00:18:11,420 --> 00:18:15,140
