upon their very own private garden.

310
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:14,820
Thus, I have aptly named this wondrous,
terrifying place Little Garden.

311
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,520
Louis Arnot, Explorer.

312
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:36,780
Well, what is the answer?

313
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:38,417
Could you repeat that?

314
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:39,437
I didn't catch it.

315
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:40,840
Please, sir?

316
00:19:42,980 --> 00:19:44,920
I asked if you had any alcohol.

317
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,120
I drank mine.

318
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:48,540
We have a little.

319
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:49,900
Oh, you do?

320
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:51,200
That's perfect.

321
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:52,537
Um, there's just one thing.

322
00:19:52,620 --> 00:19:53,837
It's not the drinking kind.

323
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:55,537
It's for cooking and disinfecting.

324
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:58,860
But if that's acceptable,
you're welcome to it all.

325
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:08,320
A dinosaur!

326
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:28,220
I'm Broggy, the Elbaf's
strongest warrior, Invincible!

327
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:38,660
Now I have dinner, and the two
of you are invited as my guests!

328
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:40,450
Hehehehe!

329
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:42,690
Huh?

330
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:45,100
You okay?

331
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:48,100
Just pretend you're dead.

332
00:20:48,300 --> 00:20:50,517
No matter what happens,
don't move a muscle.

333
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:52,482
That plain dad only fools bears.

334
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:53,640
It won't work.

335
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,470
Huh?

336
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,070
Huh.

337
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,050
Whoa!

338
00:21:04,133 --> 00:21:05,540
What an amazing view!

339
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:10,680
This is the perfect spot for our lunch.

340
00:21:11,580 --> 00:21:13,697
