341
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:15,600
We need to keep moving. Huh?

342
00:21:16,820 --> 00:21:19,420
Oh, they have active volcanoes here.

343
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:23,520
Not only that, look, there's a
mountain with huge holes in it.

344
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,560
It's dangerous up there.

345
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:27,739
Come down already.

346
00:21:36,820 --> 00:21:38,580
Let me know! This is awful!

347
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:40,289
He's been eating the lawn!

348
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:42,940
Oh, it got dark.

349
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:45,790
Whoa!

350
00:21:45,873 --> 00:21:46,860
Oh, so hot!

351
00:21:58,480 --> 00:21:59,310
Huh?

352
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:28,070
What fun.

353
00:22:28,153 --> 00:22:29,159
That was glorious.

354
00:22:29,340 --> 00:22:31,397
Watching the likes of you
grapple with longnecks

355
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:33,757
is the most entertainment
I've had in quite a while.

356
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:36,220
You are my first visitor in a long time.

357
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:38,840
Wow, you are huge! Are you human?

358
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:44,186
Greatest warrior of all Elba!

359
00:22:44,380 --> 00:22:45,320
I am Dory!

360
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:49,570
It's a...

361
00:22:49,653 --> 00:22:50,483
a giant!

362
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:55,600
I've heard that they exist, but
I've never actually seen one before.

363
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:57,520
Well, hi, I'm Luffy!

364
00:22:57,760 --> 00:22:58,717
And I'm a pirate!

365
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:01,330
A pirate?

366
00:23:01,413 --> 00:23:03,125
Well, good for you, my friend!

367
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:06,370
Gah, gah,

368
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:19,100
gah,

369
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:21,130
gah,

370
00:23:21,213 --> 00:23:22,043
gah, gah, gah,

371
00:23:22,126 --> 00:23:24,417
gah, gah, gah, gah, gah,

372
00:23:26,693 --> 00:23:30,120
gah, gah,

373
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:32,660
g

374
00:23:42,060 --> 00:23:44,200
Go on, eat hearty, my friends.

375
00:23:44,460 --> 00:23:45,636
It tastes delicious.

376
00:23:48,600 --> 00:23:50,820
I think I've lost my appetite.

377
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:53,220
Don't be shy now. Dig in.

378
00:23:55,220 --> 00:23:56,900
No, I don't want to eat.

379
00:23:57,620 --> 00:23:58,450
Huh?

380
00:23:59,300 --> 00:24:00,653
Dinosaur meat is sweet.

381
00:24:00,780 --> 00:24:02,604
I promise you it's quite tasty.

382
00:24:03,380 --> 00:24:06,997
Well, I guess he's attempting to
fatten us up before he kills us.

383
00:24:07,080 --> 00:24:08,600
We'll be plump and juicy.

384
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:10,737
I never thought he'd end like this.

385
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:12,720
He's a typical barbaric giant.

386
00:24:13,340 --> 00:24:15,860
We're too young to die. Too young.

387
00:24:16,220 --> 00:24:17,660
Maybe that's the appeal.

388
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:19,150
Well, wait.

389
00:24:19,420 --> 00:24:20,360
It's too bad.

390
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:23,636
You don't know what a
scrumptious meal you're missing.

391
00:24:24,060 --> 00:24:26,200
We can't eat until the log resets.

392
00:24:26,420 --> 00:24:29,797
If we can keep our hunger and
waistlines in check, we might survive.

393
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:32,837
Yeah, but I don't know how much
longer I can hold out, Nami.

394
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:34,617
If I don't eat something pretty soon,

395
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:38,759
I'm not sure I'll have the strength
or willpower to resist his offer.

396
00:24:40,660 --> 00:24:41,490
Loggy, sir?

397
00:24:42,060 --> 00:24:44,178
Do you mind if I ask you a question?

398
00:24:45,280 --> 00:24:47,077
What's on your mind, young lady?

399
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:50,572
Um, how long will it take to
reset the log on this island?

400
00:24:51,580 --> 00:24:52,800
One full year.

401
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:56,630
A year?

402
00:24:57,260 --> 00:25:00,977
If we waited that long to eat, we
wouldn't have stomachs to feed.

403
00:25:01,060 --> 00:25:01,890
It's over.

404
00:25:01,973 --> 00:25:03,372
We have to admit defeat.

405
00:25:03,980 --> 00:25:06,627
Don't tell me you're
gonna fall asleep again.

406
00:25:18,620 --> 00:25:20,760
You sure know how to cook, Giant.

407
00:25:21,540 --> 00:25:23,217
Why, thanks for the compliment.

408
00:25:23,300 --> 00:25:25,417
Your pirate goodies are
excellent too, my little friend.

409
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:27,617
although the portions are a little small.

410
00:25:28,820 --> 00:25:30,357
Yeah, I know what you mean.

411
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:34,737
But the chef on my ship made it especially
for this trip, so I'm glad you liked it?

412
00:25:34,820 --> 00:25:36,477
because otherwise I'd have to beat you up.

413
00:25:37,473 --> 00:25:39,740
Was that a threat, shorty? Ah!

414
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:43,020
I like you, little pirate.

415
00:25:43,180 --> 00:25:44,417
You're really funny.

416
00:25:44,500 --> 00:25:45,330
Hey!

417
00:25:45,413 --> 00:25:46,905
They're becoming fast friends.

418
00:25:47,340 --> 00:25:51,017
I don't mean to pry, but why do you
choose to live out here all by yourself?

419
00:25:51,100 --> 00:25:53,335
Don't you have a village to call home?

420
00:25:53,560 --> 00:25:57,480
I came from a village, a place
of many warriors, called Elbath.

421
00:25:57,640 --> 00:26:00,217
It once was home, but I
no longer call it that.

422
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:01,130
Why?

423
00:26:01,213 --> 00:26:04,175
There are certain rules in
Elbath which must be obeyed.

424
00:26:04,520 --> 00:26:05,737
Hmm, what kind of rules?

425
00:26:05,820 --> 00:26:09,291
For example, if a fight breaks
out and neither side yields,

426
00:26:09,760 --> 00:26:11,717
judgment is handed down by Elbath's god.

427
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:14,977
Whoever he deems to be
righteous will be declared

428
00:26:15,060 --> 00:26:17,757
the winner and granted
survival as well as divine

429
00:26:17,840 --> 00:26:20,657
protection so Elbeth's
God decides that doesn't

430
00:26:20,740 --> 00:26:24,437
seem fair fair or not all
that matters is this is

431
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:27,597
our battleground as on
Elbeth our God will decide

432
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:29,737
who was righteous and
worthy of winning both the

433
00:26:29,820 --> 00:26:33,617
duel and his life yeah yeah
yeah yeah we fought for

434
00:26:33,700 --> 00:26:36,680
a century but Elbeth has
yet to choose a Champion,

435
00:26:38,380 --> 00:26:40,937
You guys have been fighting
for more than a hundred years?

436
00:26:41,020 --> 00:26:44,217
From a human's point of view, 100
years may seem like a long time,

437
00:26:44,300 --> 00:26:47,657
but it isn't considering a giant's
average lifespan is three times yours.

438
00:26:49,320 --> 00:26:50,677
Even with all the time in the world,

439
00:26:50,760 --> 00:26:54,057
I think your desire would wane after
a hundred years of the same battle.

440
00:26:54,140 --> 00:26:57,097
At this point, is there any
real animosity left between you?

441
00:26:57,180 --> 00:26:58,997
Or are you just fighting to fight?

442
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:10,140
Wow, that's some explosion.

443
00:27:11,260 --> 00:27:13,300
Well then, it's time to get going.

444
00:27:21,320 --> 00:27:23,640
What was that? An eruption.

445
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:28,430
Huh?

446
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:33,680
I don't like that look.

447
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:34,957
He seems angry.

448
00:27:35,040 --> 00:27:39,360
Please forgive me, but there
is something I must attend to.

449
00:27:40,040 --> 00:27:41,800
What? You're leaving?

450
00:27:42,260 --> 00:27:43,400
No choice.

451
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:47,897
That's the signal my opponent and I
used to mark the beginning of our fight.

452
00:27:47,980 --> 00:27:50,700
A fight? With who? Where?

453
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:52,409
And more importantly, why?

454
00:27:53,180 --> 00:27:54,010
Why?

455
00:27:54,093 --> 00:27:55,080
I don't remember!

456
00:27:58,640 --> 00:28:01,600
And before we realized,
it became our routine.

457
00:28:02,300 --> 00:28:04,020
That volcano is our marker.

458
00:28:04,260 --> 00:28:05,966
Whenever it erupts, we begin.

459
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:07,800
It's senseless.

460
00:28:08,140 --> 00:28:12,157
How could you have so much hatred for
someone that you'd fight them for a century?

461
00:28:12,240 --> 00:28:14,946
What could have happened
to make you this mad?

462
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:17,150
Vivi, that's enough.

463
00:28:17,233 --> 00:28:19,298
That's not what this is about, okay?

464
00:28:26,560 --> 00:28:27,390
You're right.

465
00:28:27,580 --> 00:28:28,756
This is about honor.

466
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:39,160
I have forgotten!

467
00:28:41,540 --> 00:28:43,820
The reason for our brawl!

468
00:29:01,600 --> 00:29:04,417
The odds that you'll
find it are slim to none.

469
00:29:04,500 --> 00:29:07,757
The world's such a big
place, the oceans are wide.

470
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:11,664
Tomocopo won't help you find it,
just give up, it's astronomical.

471
00:29:14,040 --> 00:29:15,099
If you've been so!

472
00:29:18,060 --> 00:29:21,077
If someone tries to
keep us from moving on!

473
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:24,397
The factor behind our
back just keeps us strong.

474
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:29,397
It's too bad cause we're still
selling for what's so fun for y 'all?

475
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:31,157
Just leave us alone.

476
00:29:31,240 --> 00:29:35,017
It may be for this
chasing impossible things.

477
00:29:35,100 --> 00:29:37,477
But I've just gotta try.

478
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:43,620
The crazier the dream The
more ambition I'm gonna need.

479
00:29:44,180 --> 00:29:50,737
It may be for this driving home But
I know that I've just gotta fly.

480
00:29:50,820 --> 00:29:56,900
We'll follow the sea The greater
paradise We're gonna fly.

481
00:29:58,300 --> 00:30:00,217
Don't give up, just keep up crying.

482
00:30:00,300 --> 00:30:02,420
And you say that you're closer to

483
00:30:03,180 --> 00:30:05,160
The horizon of your dreams?
